for decades the so-called space race was  dominated by superpowers pouring  government funds  into conquering the final frontier now  it's all about  billionaires like richard branson elon  musk and jeff bezos  each have formed their own companies  vying for lucrative contracts  and plans to take tourists beyond  earth's orbit  so far none of the tycoons has boarded  their own rockets  next month bezos plans to change that i  want to go on this flight  because it's a thing i've wanted to do  all my life  the launch planned for july the 20th  will see bezos his brother  and the winner of an online auction  climb aboard a new shepard rocket  if all goes well the 11 minute flight  will see the passengers reach the edge  of space  before returning to earth it's being  seen by many as a potential triumph over  rivals  branson and musk so yeah there's  probably a little bit of like ego  involved but  but there's probably genuine passion  there too i mean all all  like three of these people have been at  this now for the better part of  of two decades so i think yeah i mean i  think there is like genuine interest and  like genuine passion there too  that passion has come at a price for all  three entrepreneurs but former  astronauts say  these commercial projects could make  space flight a reality for those that  can afford it  i don't know if space travel in our  lifetimes is ever going to become  quite as as popular as airplane travel  but nevertheless  it's going to give a lot more people the  opportunity to experience  what i and my fellow astronauts have  experienced the new shepard rocket has  successfully carried out 15 missions to  the edge of space  albeit without passengers with bezos on  board the new space race  could be about to get even more  competitive  the rivalry between jeff bezos and elon  musk has been  simmering for years their sparring  matches on social media are there for  all to see  but in marketing terms this could be a  victory for the founder of amazon  question is what will elon musk do to  top his rival's  latest move no one knows but the world  is watching andy gallacher al-jazeera  miami florida
 

